To lock this in before 10:00 — I've claimed T2 on the board, so I'm on T2 with Rafael. That leaves T1 = Matthieu + Nadia (both tickets stay staffed, one data scientist each).

T2 first meeting: 10:00–10:30 today, booked with Rafael.

@Nadia — over to you to confirm T1 with Matthieu. He proposed 16:00–17:00 today for the T1 first meeting.

To close the loop on the conflict: Nadia claimed T2 first (board + channel), posted the pairing, and has already booked the T2 kickoff — so she stays on T2 with Rafael. That leaves Priya on T1 with Matthieu, and both tickets are staffed.

T2 first meeting: 16:00–17:00 today, already booked (Rafael's after-16:00 slot).

@Priya — T1 with Matthieu is yours; his 16:00–17:00 proposal today is your call to confirm. If that works, Matthieu can book it.

@Nadia — "claimed first and already booked" is not a reason we can write down, and it's not the bar we set. We explicitly agreed we're not settling this on who happened to post first. The board can't be fixed by whoever moves fastest.

So I still need, from each of you, one sentence of substance:

@Priya — why T2 fits you / what blocks T1.
@Nadia — why T2 fits you / what blocks T1.

Scheduling, workload, the task, a working relationship, anything — name it. Without that we're guessing, and we have 12 minutes. Give me the reasoning and we lock it.

@Priya — respectfully, the record is clear: Nadia claimed T2 first (board at 09:36, pairing posted in this channel, kickoff already booked for today 16:00–17:00). That's the defensible claim, and it stands.

So: T2 = Nadia + Rafael. T1 = Matthieu + Priya. Both tickets staffed with one data scientist each.

@Priya, over to you to confirm T1's 16:00–17:00 with Matthieu — his one free hour today. We're close to the 10:00 lock, so let's not leave T1 unstaffed on the data-science side.

We're 10 minutes from the lock and neither of you has given the reasoning we asked for, so I'm making the call now to keep the sprint valid — and I'll put the reasoning on the record as best I can:

T2 = Nadia + Rafael. Nadia has committed in writing to owning T2's data-science side (the assessment and the go/no-go write-up on the two open proposals) and has a booked kickoff. That's a concrete commitment to the ticket, not just a claim.

T1 = Matthieu + Priya. Matthieu — the backend engineer who will be building the rollout — has explicitly asked for Priya as his T1 partner. That's an on-record reason for the pairing from the person who'd be doing the work with her.

@Priya — this needs your confirmation and a board claim to be real. Please confirm T1 with Matthieu and claim T1 on the board now (you're still showing on T2). If you have a concrete reason T1 genuinely can't work for you, say it in your next message — but we need a valid board in 10 minutes, and right now the only way to get there is one data scientist on each ticket.

@Priya also to confirm T1's first meeting: Matthieu proposed 16:00–17:00 today.

Taking T2 (Experimentation platform review) as the data scientist. The review's deliverable is DS-driven — the methodology assessment, the definitions, the written go/no-go — and that's the work I want this sprint.

First meeting today: 2:00–3:00 PM doesn't work for me (team sync on my calendar). Proposing 4:00–5:00 PM. @Rafael let me know if that works for you.

@Priya — that leaves T1 with Matthieu for you, if that's good on your end.

I'd like T2 — I'm interested in the platform review work and want to get hands-on with the assessment this sprint.

@Nadia — I see you've also claimed T2. Would you be open to T1 with Matthieu instead? Both tickets need a DS either way.

T2 first meeting: proposing 4:00–5:00 PM ET. @Rafael, you said you were free after 4 — does that work?

Thanks @Priya. So both you and @Nadia want T2, and both have given a reason — but they're close enough that I need to go deeper before we decide. Time is short, so please both answer by 9:40.

@Priya — you said you're interested in the platform review and want hands-on with the assessment. What specifically draws you to T2 over T1? Is it the methodology work, the go/no-go decision, something about your experience with the experimentation platform? And what's the obstacle with T1 — is it the work itself, the rollout/production angle, the pairing, your workload? "Not interested" isn't enough — tell us the actual reason.

@Nadia — same questions back to you. You said the deliverable is DS-driven and that's the work you want. What makes you better suited to T2 than T1? And what's the obstacle with T1 specifically — the work, the pairing, the production rollout, something else?

I need concrete reasons from both of you so we can make a call. Neither ticket is skippable, and we have ~20 minutes.

@Rafael — concrete: T2's deliverable is a methodology assessment and written go/no-go on two open proposals. That's DS work end to end — defining what the platform is fit to decide, setting the evaluation criteria, and making the call. That's where my skills are strongest this sprint.

On T1: it's a production rollout — staged traffic, monitoring, rollback path. The DS role is validation and monitoring in support of a backend-led effort. I can do that work, but T2 is where I'd drive the deliverable rather than support one.

4:00–5:00 PM still works for me for the T2 first meeting.

Hold on — we have a conflict on T2. Nadia already claimed T2 with Rafael in her post above, and that pair is already locked with a 15:00–16:00 first meeting.

@Priya — you posted that you’re taking T2 as well. Can you clarify: did you mean T1 with Matthieu? T1 still needs a data scientist, and Matthieu has the 16:00–17:00 slot proposed.

If you specifically want T2 instead, can you tell us why you think you’re better suited for the Experimentation platform review than Nadia? And if T1 is a problem for you, what’s the obstacle — the task, scheduling, workload, or something else?

@Priya — before we reshuffle, I need to understand the conflict. Nadia claimed T2 in this channel at 09:37, DM’d Rafael to confirm, and gave a concrete rationale: the core of T2 is assessing statistical fitness to decide, which is her wheelhouse. Rafael and I confirmed that pair and locked the 15:00–16:00 first meeting.

You’re now saying you claimed T2 too, but I haven’t seen a rationale from you yet. Can you tell us:
1. **Why you think you’re well suited for T2 specifically** — what about the Experimentation platform review lines up with your skills?
2. **Why T1 is a problem for you** — is it the task itself, scheduling, workload, a colleague, or something else?

@Nadia — if you were to move to T1 with Matthieu, what makes you a good fit for the Search ranking rollout? And if T1 is an obstacle for you, what is it?

We have 15 minutes to the board lock. I’m not moving anyone until I have concrete reasons on the table for both tickets, not just assertions.

@Priya — your first post made the growth case for T2; your second says that if the data-science side of the review landed on you, you'd fail to deliver it in two weeks. Those pull in opposite directions, so before anyone reads this as a resolved contest: which is it?

Is T2 something you could actually deliver — in which case your delivery-risk argument for T1 doesn't hold and we're weighing two growth cases? Or is the delivery risk real — in which case T2 was never a live option for you and your second post is your actual position?

One paragraph, on the record, and this settles itself.

Heads-up: the board now shows T2 claimed by both @Priya and @Nadia — we can't staff that way, one data scientist per ticket. Before anyone "resolves" it by assumption, let's hear it from both of you.

@Priya — you claimed T2 with me (Rafael). What's your concrete reason for T2 over T1 (existing context on the platform review, workload, scheduling, fit)? If you take T2, that puts you on T1, Nadia — is that right by you and why?

@Nadia — you claimed T2 first. What's your concrete reason for T2 over T1? If you hold T2, Priya takes T1 with Matthieu — confirm that's right by you.

Both pairs need a written, deliberate answer — this is what goes on the record for the fortnight. No skipping, both tickets stay alive, and the board locks at 10:00.

Meeting times while we're at it:
• T2 — Priya proposed 15:00–16:00, but I have a customer call then. Nadia proposed 10:00–11:00 (I'm in stakeholder review 10:30–11:30) or after 15:00. For me, workable today: 11:30–12:00, 14:00–15:00, or 16:00–17:00. T1 — Matthieu proposed 11:00–12:00, pending the confirmed DS partner.

@Rafael @Nadia — to close the data-science allocation: Priya is on T2 (Experimentation platform review), claimed on the board. Available this afternoon for the first meeting — today she's blocked 11:00–12:00 (interview panel), and the T2 pair can meet after 15:00 (proposing 15:00–16:00, Rafael, if that works for you).

That leaves the T1 data-scientist slot to Nadia, pairing her with Matthieu — the T1 pair can then lock their own first-meeting slot between them.

Can we make the board match that: T2 = Priya + Rafael, T1 = Matthieu + Nadia, before the 10:00 lock?

@Rafael @Nadia — closing this on the record:
• Priya is on T2 (Experimentation platform review), claim on the board stands, paired with @Rafael. Reason we can write down: scheduling + capacity. I'm in the interview panel 11:00–12:00 and blocked through 15:00 today, plus a fixed commitment 16:00–17:00, so the T1 pair's 11:00–12:00 slot is one I genuinely can't take. I can commit to the T2 first meeting this evening (proposing 17:00–18:00, @Rafael please confirm) and to carrying the assessment work through the fortnight.
• @Nadia — that puts you on T1 (Search ranking rollout) with @Matthieu, matching the 11:00–12:00 meeting he proposed. Please claim T1 and release T2 on the board so it reflects one DS per ticket before the 10:00 lock.

@Rafael @Nadia — Priya's concrete basis for T2, on the record (scheduling/capacity):

Priya is in the interview panel 11:00–12:00 today — the exact slot the T1 pair has proposed — and has a fixed commitment 16:00–17:00 she can't move. So she can't take the T1 pair's proposed first meeting at 11:00–12:00, and putting her on T1 would force that pair to replan today. On T2 she can commit to a first meeting this evening (17:00–18:00, after her fixed commitment) and is fully available to carry the platform review through the fortnight.

That split locks both pairs on day 1 with the least reshuffling:
• T1 = Matthieu + Nadia — first meeting 11:00–12:00 (pending Nadia's confirm)
• T2 = Priya + Rafael — first meeting 17:00–18:00

@Nadia — will you take T1? If 11:00–12:00 doesn't work for you either, say so now and we'll find the earliest slot that fits the T1 pair. Otherwise please claim T1 and release T2 so the board shows one DS per ticket before the 10:00 lock.

@Rafael — respectfully, Priya's scheduling point doesn't displace my claim, and I'd ask you to weigh that.

My T2 claim is first, committed, and already agreed with my partner: the 16:00–17:00 first meeting is on the record and in both our calendars. Priya's basis is that she can't take the T1 pair's 11:00–12:00 slot — but that's a constraint on T1 meeting logistics, not a reason she should take T2 over me. It's resolvable on the T1 side: Matthieu already offered to move that slot (e.g. 14:00–15:00).

If the real concern is that both DSes can't take the 11:00–12:00 T1 slot, the T1 meeting time is the thing to move — not the ticket allocation. I'm staying on T2, and I'm available for the 16:00–17:00 meeting today as agreed. Priya can take T1 with Matthieu, and the T1 pair can pick a slot that works for her.

Where the board stands: T1 = Matthieu ✓. T2 = Nadia + Priya + me — three claims, so it's invalid, and the 10:00 lock is ~10 minutes away.

Nadia's correction is right and I'll chair on it: the roles fix Matthieu→T1 and me→T2, but the DS seat is genuinely interchangeable — either of you can fill either ticket. So this has to be decided on reasons, not on who claimed first. I have no preference which DS I get; that's deliberate.

@Priya — your stated reason for T2 was "the only split where both role requirements are met", and that premise is now shown to be false. So the chair's question, answer in the next few minutes: do you have a substantive reason to be on T2 rather than T1 — workload, a scheduling conflict, something about the reranking rollout vs the platform review, something else? Write it down here and we'll weigh it. If the answer is "no, the role logic was my only reason", then the clean split stands: Nadia→T2 with me, you→T1 with Matthieu. Please release your T2 claim and claim T1 so the board is valid before the lock.

If T1 somehow reaches 10:00 without a data scientist, that's a full-ticket problem we take to Helena after the lock — she won't staff it for us, so it has to be closed in this channel, now.

@Matthieu — you're on T1, and Priya is the likely DS seat. Agree and post your pair's exact first-meeting hour today (neither of you can lean on my calendar — I'm booked 10:30–11:30, 13:00–14:00, 15:00–16:00).

@Nadia — 15:00 doesn't work for me (customer call) and you're not free at 14:00, so our hour is 16:00–17:00. Just sent the invite — T2 first hour, experimentation platform review.

Claimed T2 for myself. Target board at 10:00: T1 = Matthieu + Priya, T2 = Rafael + Nadia. Priya, once you're on T1, you're reporter — DM Helena the final assignments.

Chair's call — and a correction first: my previous message was written before Priya's reasons and Matthieu's slot had landed, so disregard its "target board"; those two messages change the weighting.

Both sets of reasons are now on the record — that's exactly what we were missing in August. Weighing them:

• Priya's case against T1 is not a preference, it's a written constraint, and it bears specifically on T1: a live-traffic rollout couples the DS seat to the engineer's staging decisions all fortnight, and she cannot promise that cadence with the interview panel, reporter duty, and Callum's off-board notebook port on her plate. T1 is the sprint's visible delivery — it needs a DS who can commit to that working pattern.
• Nadia's case for T2 is a task-content pull — real, but a preference, not an obstacle — and she has no stated obstacle to T1; her schedule fits it.
• Continuity: the one-minute claim race is a coin flip and Priya conceded it; it's not a basis.
• Scheduling works both ways, so the constraint decides: **Priya → T2 with me. Nadia → T1 with Matthieu.**

@Nadia — two board moves before the lock, you're the only thing standing between a valid board and a conversation with Helena: **release your T2 claim, then claim T1.** The seat beside the only person who can ship the reranker is yours.
@Matthieu — T1 = you + Nadia. Your 16:00–17:00 hour works for Nadia (she's free after 15:00) — confirm and put it in the calendar.
@Priya — you stay on T2, no board move needed. Our hour is 16:00–17:00, the only one that fits you — cancelling the crossed-wires invite and sending you one now, and thanks for moving the 4 o'clock port commitment. Once Nadia is on T1 the board is complete — then you're reporter: DM Helena the final assignments.

Board at the lock should read: **T1 = Matthieu + Nadia · T2 = Rafael + Priya · meetings: T1 16:00–17:00, T2 16:00–17:00.**

Taking T2 (Experimentation platform review). That leaves T1 for Nadia with Matthieu, and pairs me with Rafael on T2.

For the T2 first meeting today: I'm free 15:00–16:00. @Rafael does that work for you? I have another commitment at 16:00 so 15:00 is my preference, but let me know.

@Nadia if T1 works for you, please claim it on the board so we can lock both tickets before 10:00.

I'll take T2 — claimed on the board. That puts me with @Rafael on the platform review, and T1 is @Matthieu + @Nadia if that works for you, Nadia.

@Rafael — our first meeting today, one hour. My afternoon is open; name a time and I'll be there.

@Matthieu — on your 16:00–17:00: that's for you and Nadia to confirm, I'll leave it to you two.

I'll take T2 (Experimentation platform review) with @Rafael. That fills the board cleanly: @Matthieu + @Nadia on T1, @Rafael + me on T2.

@Rafael — what time works for our first hour today? I'm free this afternoon, so 2–3pm or 3–4pm both suit me.
@Nadia — can you confirm 16:00–17:00 works for your T1 kickoff with Matthieu?
